title: President Ebert must appoint a new government!
subtitle: Hopefully this new government will last...
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1925 and month >= 1 and weimar_coalition = 0
max-visits: 1

= President Ebert must appoint a new Chancellor!

The December 1924 elections produced a divided Reichstag and the current Chancellor, Wilhelm Marx, has thus far proved unable to find a majority. While whatever government forms must be acceptable to a majority in the Reichstag, the President’s role in appointing the Chancellor gives us sway should we choose to use it.

- @appointment_menu: Let us begin.

@appointment_menu

Chancellor Marx has offered his resignation as Chancellor following his failure to bring together a governing coalition.

Will we accept his resignation?

- @resignation_yes: Yes, we will accept his resignation – This is the Historical Option.
- @resignation_no: No, he must stay on.

@resignation_no

We have refused Marx’s resignation, however this brings us no closer to an actual governing coalition.

What form of government should we recommend he pursue?

- @Marx_Right: A Right Coalition including the DNVP?
- @Marx_Grand: A Grand Coalition including the SPD?
- @Marx_Minority: A Minority Bourgeois Coalition, with SPD toleration?

@Marx_Right
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: The DNVP prefers other candidates for Chancellor.

@Marx_Grand
choose-if: never
unavailable-subtitle: The DVP is unwilling.

@Marx_Minority
choose-if: grand_coalition >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Somehow, even this arrangement does not have enough votes.
subtitle: A minority government is undesirable, but perhaps necessary.

Marx has agreed to pursue this course of action, but many within our own party fail to see the benefit of any such arrangement. 

- @koch_weser: Appoint Koch Weser (DDP) instead as a more acceptable candidate 
- @article_48
- @marx_still: Stick with Marx and offer concessions 

@koch_weser
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 1; chancellor = "Koch-Weser"; chancellor_party = "DDP"

@marx_still
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 1; welfare += 1;

In return for concessions on Welfare, the SPD finally agrees and a minority coalition is formed under Wilhelm Marx.

@resignation_yes

The Bourgeois parties have reached an agreement with the right-wing DNVP to form a coalition under the independent Hans Luther. For any such agreement to go through, we must agree to appoint Luther, however. Will we?

- @luther_yes: Yes, we will. - This is the historical option 
- @luther_no: No, we will not permit a government containing reactionaries and anti-republicans!

@luther_no 
on-arrival: dvp_relation -= 10; dnvp_relation -= 10 ; z_relation -= 5

We have refused to appoint Luther, to the anger of the right-wing parties. Our refusal brings us no closer to forming a government, however.

Will we take matters into our own hands and appoint a Chancellor ourselves?

- @appoint_yes: Yes, we must take matters into our own hands.
- @deadlock: No, we will only appoint a transitional Chancellor

@appoint_yes 

The DVP are reluctant about any grand coalition, but perhaps they will change their tune if offered the Chancellorship.

- @jarres_grand: Appoint Karl Jarres, the Vice-Chancellor (DVP)?
- @stresemann_grand: Appoint former Chancellor Gustav Stresemann (DVP)?
- @minority_government: Could a minority government work?

@minority_government

- @reappoint_marx: Re-appoint Marx (Z)
- @koch_weser: Appoint Erich Koch-Weser (DDP)
- @coo: Let us consider our options

@coo

- @luther_yes: Appoint Luther (I) after all.
- @reappoint_marx: Reappoint Marx (Z)
- @jarres_grand: Appoint Jarres (DVP)
- @stresemann_grand: Appoint Stresemann (DVP)
- @koch_weser: Appoint Koch-Weser (DDP)
- @deadlock: Let us appoint a transitional chancellor

@reappoint_marx

We have reappointed Marx, however this brings us no closer to an actual governing coalition.

What form of government should we recommend he pursue?

- @Marx_Right: A Right Coalition including the DNVP?
- @Marx_Grand: A Grand Coalition including the SPD?
- @Marx_Minority: A Minority Bourgeois Coalition, with SPD toleration?

@deadlock

- @transitional_jarres: Jarres, the Vice-Chancellor, is a logical option for transitional Chancellor.
- @transitional_gessler: Gessler, the Reichswehr Minister, is respected – though controversial within our own party.
- @coo: Let us reconsider our options

@luther_yes
on-arrival: chancellor = "Luther"; chancellor_party = "I"; right_coalition = 1; dnvp_in_government = 1; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister = "Schiele"; interior_minister_party = "DNVP"; justice_minister = "Frenken"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Brauns"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "Gessler"; reichswehr_minister_party = "DDP"; economic_minister = "Neuhaus"; economic_minister_party = "DNVP"; finance_minister = "Schlieben"; finance_minister_party = "DNVP"; agriculture_minister = "von Kanitz"; agriculture_minister_party = "I";

We agree to appoint Hans Luther as Chancellor, even though it means the reactionary DNVP entering government. Our Left Wing are angered by this action.

@stresemann_grand
on-arrival: chancellor = "Stresemann"; chancellor_party = "DVP"; spd_in_government = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1; leverage = spd_r
go-to: election_1928.ministries

The DVP agree and a new Grand Coalition is formed under Stresemann.

@jarres_grand
on-arrival: chancellor = "Jarres"; chancellor_party = "DVP"; spd_in_government = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1; leverage = spd_r
go-to: election_1928.ministries

The DVP agree and a new Grand Coalition is formed under Jarres.

@jarres_grand
on-arrival: chancellor = "Jarres"; chancellor_party = "DVP";

We appoint Karl Jarres as a transitional Chancellor, though there is no telling how long he will be in post for…

@transitional_gessler
on-arrival: chancellor = "Gessler"; chancellor_party = "DDP"; foreign_minister = "Stresemann"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister = "Külz"; interior_minister_party = "DDP"; justice_minister = "Marx"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Brauns"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "Gessler"; reichswehr_minister_party = "DDP"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; economic_minister_party = "DVP"; finance_minister = "Luther"; finance_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister = "Haslinde"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"

We appoint Otto Gessler as a transitional Chancellor, though there is no telling how long he will be in post for…
